From: Antonio Alvarez Feijoo <antonio.feijoo@suse.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 08:44:00 +0200
Subject: fix(overlayfs-crypt): prevent eval injection in parse_overlay_opts()

parse_overlay_opts() used eval "${ns}${key}='${val}'" to assign
parsed options from the rd.overlay.crypt kernel cmdline parameter.
A single quote in the value breaks out of the assignment and allows
arbitrary command execution.

Fixes: GHSA-wr6r-5whr-98qx
Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dracut-ng/dracut/commit/584e95bea90cedd12d9190e9b09bb45e1aa26b08
---
 modules.d/71overlayfs-crypt/overlayfs-crypt-lib.sh | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules.d/71overlayfs-crypt/overlayfs-crypt-lib.sh b/modules.d/71overlayfs-crypt/overlayfs-crypt-lib.sh
index d23ac8d..cc7927f 100755
--- a/modules.d/71overlayfs-crypt/overlayfs-crypt-lib.sh
+++ b/modules.d/71overlayfs-crypt/overlayfs-crypt-lib.sh
@@ -17,10 +17,11 @@ parse_overlay_opts() {
     for tok in "$@"; do
         key="${tok%%=*}"
         val="${tok#*=}"
+        # shellcheck disable=SC2034
         [ "$key" = "$tok" ] && val=""
         case "$key" in
             mapname | fstype | mkfs | timeout)
-                eval "${ns}${key}='${val}'"
+                eval "${ns}${key}=\${val}"
                 _RET="${_RET:+$_RET }${ns}${key}"
                 ;;
             *)
